<h2>Posthumous Postscript</h2>
<p><em>Hello again from Danny and Bethany in 2026.
Forster Lists (Dot Lists) sure have stood the test of time!
There=E2=80=99s a surprising amount of cleverness in that simple protocol:<=
/em></p>
<ol>
<li><em>Colley=E2=80=99s rule</em></li>
<li><em>Structured procrastination</em></li>
<li><em><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Getting_Things_Done" title=
=3D"Getting Things Done">GTD</a>-style review</em></li>
<li><em>Distraction logging.</em></li>
</ol>
<p><em>Colley=E2=80=99s rule is like an anytime algorithm for picking the m=
ost important task.
You start with an arbitrary default and continuously preempt it with tasks =
you want to do first.
Structured procrastion leverages your own dumb pscychology to keep you prod=
uctive despite being a little (or a lot) ADHD.
GTD-style review is the anti-staleness measure.
And, finally, distraction logging lets you capture everything that crosses =
your mind without those thoughts constantly derailing you.</em></p>
<p><em>Mark didn=E2=80=99t say a lot about that last one=E2=80=89=E2=80=94=
=E2=80=89distraction logging=E2=80=89=E2=80=94=E2=80=89and since our own pr=
evious discussion of it is currently buried in an old=20
<a href=3D"https://blog.beeminder.com/tocks" title=3D"See footnote 3 and it=
s referent">Beeminder blog post on Tocks</a>, let us end by singing its pra=
ises in the context of Forster Lists.</em></p>
<p><em>We love this aspect of Mark=E2=80=99s system, where anything that po=
ps into your head you can just add it to the list and trust that you=E2=80=
=99ll see it later.=20
Also it helps ensure the whole list doesn=E2=80=99t become something you dr=
ead even looking at.
There are ugh-y things in there but you=E2=80=99re also constantly dumping =
shiny things in.
This reduces the temptation to let yourself be distracted from the task in =
the current chain.=20
By the time a task pops up in a future chain you may decide it wasn=E2=80=
=99t important and can just cross it off.=20
But the key is that with so many unimportant tasks getting dumped in, you n=
eed to make sure important ones don=E2=80=99t die in that sea.=20
Which Forster=E2=80=99s system accomplishes beautifully.</em></p>
